==English==

===Etymology===
By analogy with {{m|en|rule out}}.

===Verb===
{{en-verb|head=[[rule]] [[in]]|rules in|ruling in|ruled in}}

# {{label|en|idiomatic|transitive}} To consider (something) as a possible option among others.
#: ''At this stage, we don't want to '''rule anything in or out.'''''

====Usage notes====
* ''Rule in'' is typically used along with [[rule out]].

====Synonyms====
* [[consider]]

====Antonyms====
* [[rule out]]

